note right of digital_literacy
<b>Topic legend</b>

digital_literacy:
Computer fundamentals; computer hardware and software; computing history;
Internet and World Wide Web; email and messaging; word processing,
spreadsheets, presentations, Web search, cloud services, online
collaboration, and social networks.

programming_foundations:
Visual block programming; programming-language principles; ANSI C;
Python scripting; VBA and macros; regular expressions; data structures.

computer_architecture:
Binary and number systems; computer arithmetic; Boolean algebra and
digital logic circuits; CPU, memory, bus, instruction sets; assembly,
machine language, and low-level programming.

operating_systems:
Operating-system structure and functions; processes and threads; CPU
scheduling; concurrency and parallelism; memory and I/O management;
file systems; shell scripting; virtualization, containers, Docker,
Kubernetes, and infrastructure- and platform-as-a-service services.

networks_distributed:
Computer networks and protocols; Internet communication; distributed
systems and distributed communication.

data_information_systems:
Database concepts; relational databases, keys, SQL, tables and queries;
large-scale datasets; information-system organization, workflows,
archiving, authorization, and administration.

security_trust:
IT security, privacy, health-data protection, workstation and network
security, cryptography, electronic identification, electronic trust
services, certified email, and digital signatures.

digital_forensics:
Digital-forensics professions and investigations; evidence acquisition,
conservation, validation, chain of custody, live acquisition, analysis,
tools, reporting, testimony, ethics, and computer, file-system, cloud,
network, mobile-device, email/social-media, and graphics forensics.

health_informatics:
Italian health-system organization; laboratory and hospital information
systems; healthcare indicators; SDO and DRG case-mix systems; electronic
health records; medical devices; EEG processing; and telemedicine.

geospatial_computing:
GIS, geographical-data management and analysis, numerical cartography,
projections, coordinate systems, representation, georeferencing, and
digital graphics.

digital_government_documents:
Electronic documents and dematerialized transactions; document
management; EU digital-transformation legislation; documentary databases;
Italian government portals and online services; and authentication.

research_and_ai:
Bibliography construction with Google Scholar, Scopus, and search engines;
LaTeX and Overleaf; machine learning for text analysis; and AI
applications, including AI-assisted VBA macro generation.
end note

